 "version": 1,
 "title": "Trance Gate Stab",
 "category": "Leads and stabs",
 "text": "Sound: chords chopped into a rhythmic stutter, sixteen pulses a bar: the gated pad stab of trance and rave. Hold a chord and it pulses in time.\n\nHow it's built: two detuned saws through the Ladder filter into a VCA. The VCA's envelope has no sustain, and a Clock's 1/16 is plugged into its RETRIG: while you hold the keys, each tick starts the envelope again, so the chord pulses. Chorus, Delay and Reverb. Four voices.\n\nPlay: hold chords.\n\nTweak: the clock's TEMPO, which clock output drives RETRIG (1/8 for half as many pulses), the envelope's DECAY (longer pulses blur together), the delay's TIME.",
